1
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:05,550
Since everyone's sheltering 
in the graveyard,

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:07,520
I guess that means you finished the trial.

3
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:10,350
Great job, Emilia-tan.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,710
Ram...

5
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:19,420
Subaru! Focus your attention 
over here for now, I suppose!

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,820
What kind of weird reaction was that?

7
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:26,260
Oh, just... Hearing you call 
me just "Subaru" is new.

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,100
I was just savoring the joy of it.

9
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,320
Save that for later, I suppose... S-Subaru.

10
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,890
Damn, you're so cute!

11
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,740
So, we're up against the Great Rabbit.
 Are you ready for this?

12
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:40,190
The contract was only just signed,

13
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:42,280
and it's one of the Three Great Mabeasts.

14
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:44,690
The contractor is a novice,

15
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:48,070
and it's been 400 years since 
I was involved in a battle.

16
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:49,550
And?

17
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,410
I'd call it the perfect handicap.

18
00:00:58,370 --> 00:00:59,710
Are you scared?

19
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,630
No, I'm not scared.

20
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:09,410
I've got Emilia behind me and you beside me.

21
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:11,970
I'm feeling stronger than ever!

22
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:13,680
That's right.

23
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,020
El Minya!

24
00:01:29,230 --> 00:01:30,730
Holy crap!

25
00:01:30,730 --> 00:01:32,210
So what should I do?!

26
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:36,480
Just keep holding my hand and 
don't leave me alone, I suppose.

27
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,220
And imagine yourself

28
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:43,380
weaving mana, shaping your power 
into arrows, and crushing the enemy

29
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:45,040
in a single, supreme attack.

30
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,100
Done!

31
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,970
Then all that's left is 
to say it, I suppose!

32
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:50,000
El Minya!

33
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,120
Cross over!

34
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:55,960
Right!

35
00:01:58,810 --> 00:02:00,370
Take the left, I suppose!

36
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:02,300
Then the right's all yours!

37
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,970
Minya!

38
00:02:05,670 --> 00:02:07,330
Minya! Minya!

39
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,660
That's hard to say! Minya!

40
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:13,780
There's no end to them! 
Beako, what's the plan?

41
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:18,070
What we need to do is gather 
all of the Great Rabbits here.

42
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:22,770
They may be infinite, but that doesn't 
mean there's no upper limit, I suppose.

43
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:25,700
They can only multiply 
up to a certain number.

44
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:26,710
Which means...

45
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:30,340
If we can stop all of them when they 
hit that max, we can destroy them!

46
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:32,600
The question is how to do it.

47
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:36,490
It's not like the two of us 
have to solve this alone.

48
00:02:38,610 --> 00:02:40,000
Honestly...

49
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:44,710
Act as a decoy while I'm 
getting ready, I suppose.

50
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:46,280
Don't you worry.

51
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,440
There's no one in all of 
Lugunica better than me

52
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,660
when it comes to being bait 
for insanely strong enemies!

53
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,410
Hey, Great Rabbit!

54
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:03,610
It's me you want! Follow me!

55
00:03:03,610 --> 00:03:05,260
You're too slow!

56
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,330
Emilia-tan!

57
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:12,630
Beatrice and I are gonna knock 
all of these bastards out!

58
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:15,200
I'd appreciate it if you 
could help us a little!

59
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,060
Subaru?!

60
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,870
I know I'm asking too much!

61
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,860
If you can't do it, I'll just 
have to think a little harder,

62
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,090
but if you think you can, I want you to try!

63
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,580
Let's all win this together!

64
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:30,800
All right! You can count on me!

65
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:31,990
So I'll count on you!

66
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:33,820
Hell yeah! I'm on it!

67
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:43,080
Now, Emilia! Trace the line!

68
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:44,980
You're doing so well!

69
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,710
You always do!

70
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,740
I'm not letting any of you escape!

71
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:57,930
Wow...

72
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:04,640
And now you guys are the guiltylowe 
that came up one step short!

73
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:08,270
Okay, your turn to be the star,

74
00:04:08,510 --> 00:04:10,690
Great Spirit Beatrice!

75
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,780
Al Shamac!

76
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,640
We did it...

77
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,850
That was... so amazing.

78
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:48,390
I sent them to an isolated space, 
much like the forbidden library.

79
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:51,650
They'll never be able to 
come back out, I suppose.

80
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:17,500
Subaru, look.

81
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:24,980
Have you nothing to say to the 
one who just performed such a—

82
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,770
You did it!

83
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:29,790
I knew you could! I love you, Beako!

84
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:32,210
Wha... Wait! No! Let me go, I suppose!

85
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:32,210
That's my girl! You're so cute!

86
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:37,080
Beako's amazing! 
Beako's the best! Beako for life!

87
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:39,730
Su... Suba... Suba... Subaru!

88
00:05:52,210 --> 00:05:54,070
I'm sorry, Mother.

89
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,630
I couldn't keep my promise.

90
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:03,170
Yet you look as if a weight was 
lifted from your shoulders.

91
00:06:03,170 --> 00:06:05,770
You don't seem like yourself either, I suppose.

92
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:10,720
I thought an encounter with Mother 
was your clan's dearest wish.

93
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:15,100
May I ask something?

94
00:06:15,890 --> 00:06:16,620
Huh?

95
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:20,190
Did Subaru-kun turn out to 
be "that person" for you?

96
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:21,800
Hmph!

97
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,950
Subaru is not at all suited 
for that, I suppose.

98
00:06:25,350 --> 00:06:27,790
But that's just fine.

99
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:31,900
I chose Subaru, who is not 
"that person," I suppose.

100
00:06:32,590 --> 00:06:33,470
Why?

101
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:38,140
Because when I asked him to be 
"that person" for me, he laughed.

102
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:40,850
He insisted that he could 
make me happier than

103
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:44,300
some stranger I wouldn't even 
recognize could, I suppose.

104
00:06:44,770 --> 00:06:48,020
That is quite an arrogant answer.

105
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:51,020
But I don't dislike how pushy he is.

106
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,930
Are you sure about this?

107
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:55,840
You will never be number one to Subaru-kun.

108
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,900
You seem to be mistaken, I suppose.

109
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:03,500
I didn't leave the forbidden library 
because I became his number one.

110
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:08,750
I left because I want to 
make Subaru my number one.

111
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:11,250
Choose me.

112
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:18,760
No matter how old you get, you never change.

113
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,260
You're just like back then.

114
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:20,860
Huh?

115
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:25,390
You and I really haven't 
spoken enough, have we?

116
00:07:25,390 --> 00:07:28,640
Not in all the time since 
we were with Teacher.

117
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,270
Teacher?

118
00:07:32,650 --> 00:07:35,650
You're... Roswaal?

119
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:38,180
I have always been Roswaal.

120
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:40,240
No! That's not what I meant!

121
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,550
I was joking.

122
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,360
I am...

123
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:47,100
I'm Roswaal, Beatrice.

124
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:50,730
You can't mean... Soul transcription?

125
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:53,370
From Mother's pursuit of immortality?

126
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,950
But that failed!

127
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,340
The soul of another will not 
take hold in an empty vessel.

128
00:07:58,930 --> 00:08:00,850
So rather than use someone else,

129
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:04,700
you need only prepare a vessel that 
has high affinity with the soul.

130
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:11,450
Would you curse me as an inhuman monster?

131
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:19,070
Kneel down there, I suppose.

132
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,540
Right here?

133
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:25,730
Brace yourself.

134
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:34,000
Was that supposed to be 
a show of your contempt?

135
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,420
No. I neither know nor care why 
you want to be reprimanded.

136
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:42,130
That was obviously payback for burning 
down the forbidden library, I suppose!

137
00:08:46,950 --> 00:08:49,130
That would cause nothing but 
trouble for Mother, I suppose.

138
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:51,380
What do you think you're saying?!

139
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:51,380
All three of you are here?

140
00:08:50,010 --> 00:08:51,380
It would make me very happy.

141
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:52,710
Naturally, I suppose.

142
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:54,870
So said Beatrice as she echoed the 
very same words her teacher used.

143
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:54,270
Have you been getting 
along and not fighting?

144
00:08:54,870 --> 00:08:57,060
Well, I love you.

145
00:08:57,850 --> 00:08:58,930
Roswaal...

146
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:00,400
Yes?

147
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:02,990
Welcome back.

148
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:06,140
Yes... That's right.

149
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:09,520
I'm back, Beatrice.

150
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,550
And welcome home.

151
00:09:43,850 --> 00:09:45,780
They still haven't come out.

152
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,470
Yeah, but I'm sure they're fine.

153
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:51,690
You trust Beatrice so well now.

154
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:54,260
I guess you two were always 
good friends, huh?

155
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:58,420
Both now and back then, I'd have my 
reservations about calling us friends.

156
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,630
Is that Puck?

157
00:10:02,110 --> 00:10:05,660
I'd like to thank him for his help, 
but that won't work, will it?

158
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:07,010
You're right.

159
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:09,090
I guess he overdid it a bit,

160
00:10:09,090 --> 00:10:12,900
and even having this stone to occupy 
isn't enough to wake him up.

161
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:15,830
You'll definitely call him 
back someday, though.

162
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:16,640
Right?

163
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:19,410
Yes.

164
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,990
You've changed, Emilia-tan.

165
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,360
You're stronger now.

166
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:31,170
If I have, it's thanks to 
you and everyone else.

167
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,610
All I ever do is take, after all.

168
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:37,120
I need to get to a point where I 
can give back to everyone soon.

169
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:42,160
I feel like all I ever do is take, too.

170
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:46,830
By the way, Subaru... You know...

171
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:51,080
Huh? Your face just turned red super fast.

172
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,980
You okie?

173
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:54,690
I'm o-okie. Totally fine.

174
00:10:54,690 --> 00:10:58,000
Anyway, there's something 
important I wanted to discuss.

175
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,770
Y-You're being weirdly formal now.

176
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:07,530
So... you said that you... 
l-loved me, right?

177
00:11:07,530 --> 00:11:11,280
Huh? uh, yes, I did! 
I love you! A whole lot!

178
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:15,760
And that, um... makes me 
really, really happy...

179
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:20,340
But I wanted to have a proper talk.

180
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:24,000
About... well...

181
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:31,110
the baby I'm carrying in my belly!

182
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,460
Pardon?

183
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:38,100
I-I don't know if it's a boy or a girl,

184
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:40,610
but I know I have to take good care of it.

185
00:11:40,610 --> 00:11:43,300
But I don't know anything 
about this kind of thing.

186
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,930
So I knew I had to talk to the father...

187
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:49,120
E-Emilia-tan! Wait, wait! 
Seriously, wait a hot minute!

188
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,820
You just said... a baby, right?

189
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:53,250
Y-Yes!

190
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:56,300
It won't be easy with the 
royal selection going on.

191
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:58,850
But that's not the baby's fault!

192
00:11:58,850 --> 00:12:00,570
I just want to make them happy!

193
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:06,670
Emilia-tan, babies don't get 
carried to you by storks

194
00:12:06,670 --> 00:12:08,920
or grow in cabbage fields.

195
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:12,920
But when a boy and a girl kiss,
 it makes a baby, right?

196
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:14,380
Huh?!

197
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,990
I hate you, Puck!

198
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,990
I got ya!

199
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:34,780
Then...

200
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:41,990
Okay, now that we've gotten 
all of our scores settled,

201
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:45,000
I'd like to talk about 
where we go from here.

202
00:12:45,830 --> 00:12:48,400
I was sure you'd be pissed, though.

203
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,360
Don't be silly.

204
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:53,980
Even I don't think Roswaal-sama 
has nothing to apologize for.

205
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:58,300
But it's my own choice to treat him with 
kindness and respect after he's paid for—

206
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,730
You have such bizarre tastes.

207
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:04,080
With a wound that grave, what would have 
happened if I wasn't here, I suppose?

208
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,530
I am deeply grateful.

209
00:13:05,530 --> 00:13:08,600
But I would rather not be 
told whom I should love.

210
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,120
Ram ain't gonna change her mind.

211
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:16,360
But Boss, are you seriously sayin' 
this bastard's one of us now?

212
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:20,770
If not for you and these guys, it would've 
been a disaster for the village and the mansion!

213
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:22,650
And he's the one who planned all that!

214
00:13:22,650 --> 00:13:26,290
Still, we need Roswaal's strength.

215
00:13:26,290 --> 00:13:27,700
Boss...

216
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:32,090
Emilia can't compete in the royal 
selection without his support.

217
00:13:32,610 --> 00:13:35,360
It's natural that you'd 
want to get even with him,

218
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,940
but we can't just say 
goodbye and send him off.

219
00:13:37,940 --> 00:13:40,280
I don't agree with this.

220
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:43,450
I am willing to forgive the master.

221
00:13:43,450 --> 00:13:44,960
What the hell you sayin'?!

222
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:47,090
This bastard put you and the mansion in—

223
00:13:47,090 --> 00:13:50,270
Regardless, I am still alive...

224
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:53,020
because you saved me.

225
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,950
That's just hindsight!

226
00:13:55,520 --> 00:14:00,450
I have been in the master's 
care for more than ten years.

227
00:14:00,450 --> 00:14:06,010
I accepted his aid in 
achieving my own goals,

228
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:10,170
and I am here today because 
I learned so much from him.

229
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:13,470
You think your debt and your 
life are the same thing?!

230
00:14:13,470 --> 00:14:14,800
He used you and Ram to—

231
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:17,300
Sorry to interrupt this heated debate.

232
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:20,160
It's natural that Garfiel would be angry.

233
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,650
I did technically take part in 
the "purification ritual," too.

234
00:14:23,650 --> 00:14:27,550
You say "technically," but you were throwing 
some pretty hardcore punches, too.

235
00:14:27,550 --> 00:14:32,360
Anyway, how much does the 
margrave intend to yield to us?

236
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,450
I believe your concern

237
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:39,100
is when and where I might 
become your enemy again,

238
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:40,740
but you needn't worry about that.

239
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:44,450
You think I'm gonna trust 
a damn word you say?

240
00:14:44,450 --> 00:14:45,860
I suppose not.

241
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:50,720
So... I will prove it to you 
in a form that you can see.

242
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:01,240
That is an oath sealed with a curse.

243
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,840
An oath... sealed with a curse?

244
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:09,040
An agreement can take the form of 
a contract, an oath, or a covenant.

245
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:11,670
A covenant applies to all blood relatives,

246
00:15:11,670 --> 00:15:15,210
and an oath binds an individual.

247
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:17,470
I lost my battle.

248
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:22,470
Therefore, per my oath, 
I cannot harm any of you.

249
00:15:22,470 --> 00:15:25,890
If I break this promise, 
my soul will be tainted,

250
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:28,680
and my body will burn away 
in the flames of hell.

251
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:32,110
Then, I will descend into nothingness.

252
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,180
That is what this promise means.

253
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:36,690
Wh-Why would you make a 
crazy promise like that?

254
00:15:36,690 --> 00:15:39,290
That's quite a thing to say.

255
00:15:39,290 --> 00:15:42,880
Were you not the one who 
proposed such a contest to me?

256
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:45,350
That is what this mark is for.

257
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,600
And if I had screwed it up...

258
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,870
This mark would have been engraved on you,

259
00:15:49,870 --> 00:15:52,470
and if you broke the promise, 
you would burn to ashes.

260
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:53,270
That's scary!

261
00:15:53,690 --> 00:15:54,540
But still,

262
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:57,440
this means Roswaal can't betray us.

263
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,320
Garfiel, what do you say?

264
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:02,110
Young Gar.

265
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,880
What happened to Shima was her own choice.

266
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,820
Regardless of what happened to Young Ros,

267
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:14,320
it was necessary for one of us to 
act as the key to undo the barrier.

268
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:19,580
Shima said that she was not 
lonely these past ten years...

269
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:23,710
Because she had you.

270
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:25,260
I know.

271
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:28,510
Quit lookin' like you're 
about to cry, Grandma.

272
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:34,480
Swear it, Roswaal.

273
00:16:34,830 --> 00:16:38,800
Swear you'll never do the 
shit you've done again.

274
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,570
Swear it.

275
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:46,770
Never again shall I attempt 
to sacrifice anyone here

276
00:16:46,770 --> 00:16:51,120
in order to achieve something else.

277
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:56,870
I swear upon the soul of my beloved teacher.

278
00:16:57,590 --> 00:17:00,250
Not me. I can't forgive you.

279
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:04,500
You tried to do something awful 
to the people of the village!

280
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:07,130
They all trusted you, and then you...

281
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:10,140
I thought you were a good person, too!

282
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:13,060
Your words cause me pain.

283
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:19,600
But... But I don't want to be stubborn 
and make things harder for everyone.

284
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,400
So... I'm never going to forgive you!

285
00:17:24,410 --> 00:17:27,490
Not ever... But that's all.

286
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:32,080
Very good.

287
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:38,460
I'm only agreeing for my sister, 
the old hag, and this little girl.

288
00:17:38,770 --> 00:17:40,710
Don't forget that!

289
00:17:40,710 --> 00:17:42,320
Of course.

290
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:45,320
Anyone else got anything to say?

291
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:46,640
I do.

292
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,290
Okay, Emilia-tan.

293
00:17:48,290 --> 00:17:50,610
You've got the chance to 
say anything you want.

294
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:53,930
Then I'll take you up on that and say this.

295
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:56,680
You're all being very weird.

296
00:17:56,680 --> 00:18:00,520
Roswaal hasn't even done the 
most important thing yet.

297
00:18:00,930 --> 00:18:05,290
We can't end this discussion 
before he's done that.

298
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:07,150
The most important thing?

299
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:11,910
When you do something bad, you 
have to say, "I'm sorry."

300
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:19,090
You've all been telling him to do this 
and say that to prove he regrets it.

301
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:22,180
And Roswaal, you said you'd 
swear on your teacher's soul,

302
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:25,770
but isn't there something 
you should say before that?

303
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:28,710
Roswaal, did you say that 
to them, even once?

304
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:30,090
I didn't hear it.

305
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,390
Apologize, Roswaal.

306
00:18:33,390 --> 00:18:35,600
If you're gonna work with us from now on,

307
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:38,380
that's the right thing 
to do as a human being.

308
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,520
I am sorry.

309
00:18:44,390 --> 00:18:45,230
Good.

310
00:18:46,310 --> 00:18:47,740
That's enough.

311
00:19:05,710 --> 00:19:07,320
Conferment of knighthood?

312
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:09,550
They're really going all-out here.

313
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:14,050
I thought this was what you 
had awaited for a long time.

314
00:19:14,050 --> 00:19:18,560
Yeah, but isn't kinda shameless 
to do it in a rented space?

315
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:22,520
The Miload family is a branch 
of the Mathers family,

316
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:26,400
and their leader, Annerose, is 
head over heels for Emilia-sama.

317
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,740
And? You wanted to say something to me?

318
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:35,410
My goal is to reunite with my teacher.

319
00:19:35,410 --> 00:19:38,790
That's the woman who was 
in that coffin, right?

320
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:39,700
So haven't you already—

321
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:41,690
Do not misunderstand.

322
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:47,520
I wish to reunite with a teacher whose 
blood flows, who breathes and houses a soul.

323
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:50,840
That is my desire and my dearest wish.

324
00:19:50,840 --> 00:19:53,010
And is there a way to do that?

325
00:19:53,010 --> 00:19:57,050
I have lost the Tome of Wisdom, 
and I am bound by the mark of the oath.

326
00:19:57,050 --> 00:20:00,660
But I have no intention of 
giving up on my teacher.

327
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:02,520
What good is that gonna do?

328
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:04,050
It's simple.

329
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:08,400
I will continue to keep my eye on you.

330
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:14,710
You decided that you would lose 
nothing and pick up all the pieces.

331
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:20,160
You will surely continue 
to be hurt from now on.

332
00:20:20,450 --> 00:20:24,690
You will lose things over and over, 
and each time you get them back,

333
00:20:24,690 --> 00:20:26,900
you will carry on with new,
 invisible wounds.

334
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:33,170
If I lost anyone, I would not hesitate 
to reduce everything to ashes.

335
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:35,060
I will not compromise.

336
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:41,730
Nothing can lead me back to my teacher but you,
 Subaru-kun, and the path you walk.

337
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:54,390
We will now begin the ceremony 
of the conferment of knighthood.

338
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,240
Natsuki Subaru, come forward.

339
00:20:58,430 --> 00:21:00,450
Congratulations, Subaru-kun.

340
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:03,330
You've earned the praise 
of the witch's disciple.

341
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:07,590
You win... for today.

342
00:21:28,010 --> 00:21:30,690
The sun that looks down 
upon a brilliant world,

343
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:34,300
the stars that keep watch over 
the world when it sleeps,

344
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:38,520
the wind, to the water, to 
the earth, to the light,

345
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:40,590
the spirits that dwell in all things...

346
00:21:41,210 --> 00:21:44,210
The world that will accept 
you and nurture you,

347
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:46,860
the vast world into which 
you will be sent forth...

348
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:52,570
The pride that has supported you, 
protected you, and created you...

349
00:21:53,630 --> 00:21:55,600
May you find a way to 
live that will not shame

350
00:21:56,230 --> 00:21:58,260
all that watch over you,

351
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:01,020
the world that nurtures you,

352
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:03,070
and the pride that supports you.

353
00:22:03,790 --> 00:22:07,100
May you live as your heart dictates,

354
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:09,000
never fearing, never cowering, 
never hesitating.

355
00:22:10,010 --> 00:22:12,320
Have you the will to do all this,

356
00:22:12,630 --> 00:22:15,400
as all things surrounding you have done,

357
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:21,080
to swear that you will henceforth 
protect the one standing before you?

358
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:28,000
On the sun, the stars, the 
spirits, the world, my pride...

359
00:22:30,380 --> 00:22:35,630
And on my father and mother, I swear it.

360
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,220
I will protect you.

361
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:42,040
I will grant your every wish.

362
00:22:43,140 --> 00:22:45,330
My name is Natsuki Subaru...

363
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:51,100
your knight, Emilia, and yours alone.

364
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:54,890
Right.

365
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:13,100
This is nothing new, but you look 
so sexy and cute in that outfit.

366
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:14,840
Idiot.

367
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:28,810
Subaru? So this is where you were.

368
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,020
Oh, it's you, Emilia-tan.

369
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,560
I thought some angel or 
fairy had come to get me.

370
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,310
You're being weird again.

371
00:23:36,810 --> 00:23:38,730
Are you drunk or something?

372
00:23:39,010 --> 00:23:42,250
I told you before, I don't drink.

373
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:45,140
I'm only drunk on myself and 
the atmosphere right now.

374
00:23:45,140 --> 00:23:47,120
See? You <i>are</i> drunk.

375
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:51,130
Are you getting along with Roswaal?

376
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:53,280
What were you talking about 
before the ceremony?

377
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:56,850
Ah, I knew he was messing with you.

378
00:23:56,850 --> 00:23:58,750
You're so perceptive, Emilia-tan.

379
00:23:59,330 --> 00:24:01,800
I get the feeling things are gonna 
be even tougher than before.

380
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:07,680
I think Roswaal is just afraid of 
forgetting everything he's done.

381
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:11,350
That's why he acts like that 
to get everyone's attention.

382
00:24:11,350 --> 00:24:14,110
Honestly, he's such a child.

383
00:24:14,850 --> 00:24:17,470
You're amazing, Emilia-tan.

384
00:24:17,470 --> 00:24:18,520
You think so?

385
00:24:19,730 --> 00:24:20,650
Thanks.

386
00:24:21,230 --> 00:24:25,100
But I think that about you, too. I really do.

387
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:29,680
You know, Subaru...

388
00:24:30,230 --> 00:24:35,780
There's something I want 
to say to my knight later.

389
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:40,330
What a coincidence. There's a 
lot I want to say to you, too.

390
00:24:42,790 --> 00:24:45,050
Then it's a promise.

391
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:52,940
When the ceremony's over, 
we'll have an important talk.

392
00:24:53,410 --> 00:24:55,330
Would you come to my room?

393
00:24:55,330 --> 00:24:58,130
I'm a repeat offender when it 
comes to breaking promises,

394
00:24:58,130 --> 00:25:00,390
but when you invite me 
to your room at night,

395
00:25:00,390 --> 00:25:04,140
is breaking that promise even 
an option? No, it's not!

396
00:25:04,140 --> 00:25:07,020
Sorry... I'm not really sure 
what you're talking about.

397
00:25:10,950 --> 00:25:14,210
I can't wait to find out 
what we'll talk about.

398
00:25:14,730 --> 00:25:17,200
One evening might not be enough.

399
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:21,040
If it's that important, I'll give 
you as many evenings as it takes.

400
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:24,790
I'm your number one knight! Okay?

401
00:25:25,310 --> 00:25:26,910
O-Okay.

402
00:25:32,770 --> 00:25:34,800
Don't worry, Emilia-tan.

403
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:38,580
No matter what you say, I'll never 
become disenchanted with you.

404
00:25:39,350 --> 00:25:40,520
Subaru...

405
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:44,350
What's important isn't the 
beginning or the middle.

406
00:25:44,350 --> 00:25:45,660
It's the end.

407
00:25:46,180 --> 00:25:48,240
Besides, no matter what started it,

408
00:25:48,750 --> 00:25:50,990
it's not like it's still 
the same now, right?

409
00:25:51,660 --> 00:25:53,570
How... do you know?

410
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:05,090
You were looking out over the hall 
with those sweet eyes before.

411
00:26:05,090 --> 00:26:07,010
Seeing that made it obvious.

412
00:26:07,810 --> 00:26:10,220
If making that circle around you bigger

413
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:13,460
is one of your reasons for 
wanting to work so hard,

414
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:16,670
then let your number one help you.

415
00:26:18,690 --> 00:26:22,010
You really don't mind if I rely on you?

416
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:26,320
What do you think I promised 
you a minute ago?

417
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:29,020
I want you to rely on me before anyone else.

418
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:32,160
If there's anything I can 
help you with, I will,

419
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:36,350
and if there's anything you don't understand,
 I'll think about it with you.

420
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:42,990
Right.

421
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:47,780
All right, my doubts are gone now!

422
00:26:51,030 --> 00:26:54,180
Subaru, your face looks so sweet right now.

423
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:55,890
I wonder why.

424
00:26:55,890 --> 00:27:00,330
Maybe I'm just happy to see what 
you're seeing, and I think it's nice.

425
00:27:00,330 --> 00:27:02,020
Oh, I can understand that.

426
00:27:02,500 --> 00:27:05,810
It makes me happy if you 
feel the same way about it.

427
00:27:05,810 --> 00:27:09,090
I'm not so sure... 
That might not be quite right.

428
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:11,710
I do think it's okay if 
we think differently.

429
00:27:14,610 --> 00:27:17,500
It's such a nice atmosphere, 
isn't it, Emilia-tan?

430
00:27:18,330 --> 00:27:19,060
Yes.

431
00:27:22,570 --> 00:27:26,270
I think this scene just might be my ideal.

432
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:29,420
I'll never forget it.

433
00:27:39,420 --> 00:27:49,420


434
00:27:56,330 --> 00:28:00,830
Offbeat Steps Under the Moonlight

